Taxonomy: US GAAP 2026
**/

rule-name-prefix DQC

/** V30 Release **/

/**
Overview: 11-K filings (Employee Stock Purchase, Savings and Similar Plans) often involve more than one legal entity, such as the plan itself and the employer/plan sponsor. SEC EDGAR XBRL guidance requires that the cover page DocumentType and AmendmentFlag elements of an 11-K filing be tagged with a member on the LegalEntityAxis so that data consumers can determine which legal entity the filing pertains to.

Rule US.0248.10960 checks that, for 11-K, 11-K/A and 11-KT filings, both the DocumentType and AmendmentFlag elements have been reported with a member on the LegalEntityAxis somewhere in the filing. The rule fires if either element has not been tagged with a LegalEntityAxis member.
**/

ASSERT US.0248.10960 SATISFIED

$rule_id = (rule-name().split('.'))[rule-name().split('.').length];

/** DQCRT RULE **/
if not applicable_form(rule-name())
	skip
else

$EBPReports = set('11-K','11-K/A','11-KT').contains([covered @concept.local-name ='DocumentType']);

if not $EBPReports
	skip
else
	$documentTypeFact = first(list([covered @concept.local-name = 'DocumentType']));
	$amendmentFlagFact = first(list([covered @concept.local-name = 'AmendmentFlag']));

	/** An element is considered properly tagged if any instance of that concept anywhere in the filing carries a LegalEntityAxis member **/
	$documentTypeHasLegalEntity = exists({covered @concept = $documentTypeFact.concept where $fact.dimensions.keys.name.local-name.contains('LegalEntityAxis')});

	$amendmentFlagHasLegalEntity = not exists($amendmentFlagFact) or exists({covered @concept = $amendmentFlagFact.concept where $fact.dimensions.keys.name.local-name.contains('LegalEntityAxis')});

	$missingElements = list(for $checkItem in list(list('DocumentType', $documentTypeHasLegalEntity), list('AmendmentFlag', $amendmentFlagHasLegalEntity))
								if $checkItem[2]
									skip
								else
									$checkItem[1])

	$missingElements.length > 0

message
"The filing has a DocumentType of {$documentTypeFact} which identifies it as an 11-K filing (Employee Stock Purchase, Savings and Similar Plans), but the following cover page element(s) are not tagged with a member on the LegalEntityAxis anywhere in the filing: {$missingElements.join(', ')}.

11-K filings often involve more than one legal entity, such as the plan itself and the employer or plan sponsor. SEC EDGAR XBRL guidance requires that the cover page be tagged to a specific legal entity using the LegalEntityAxis so that data consumers can determine which entity the filing pertains to. Without this tagging, data consumers cannot determine the legal context of the filing, resulting in ambiguity in automated data extraction and analysis.

The filer should report {$missingElements.join(' and ')} with a member on the LegalEntityAxis identifying the entity to which the filing pertains.

Rule Element Id:{$rule_id}
Rule version: {$ruleVersion}"

severity error

rule-focus $documentTypeFact

effectiveDate $effective_dates[$rule_id]
